 "product_type": "forecast",
 "bottom_line": "<p>The most dangerous areas are steep, planar slopes generally above 12,000 feet on the north half of the compass, where thicker slabs rest on old, weak snow from early to mid-October. Previous wind loading and slightly stiffer snow surfaces are good clues to potentially more dangerous slopes. Consider the outcome of even a small sluff or wind pocket that knocks you off your feet if you choose to ride in steep, consequential terrain. </p>",
